    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0504" n="388" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg388"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100K77/79.]</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Dominican
                        Minister</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-03-07">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg your acceptance of my appreciative
                    thanks for your thoughtful courtesy in communicating to me, which you did by
                    your note of the 4th instant, the text of the cablegram which you received from
                    your Government concerning the visit of the Secretary of State to the Dominican
                    Republic.</p>
                <p>I can not but express to you my satisfaction at the cordial welcome which it
                    conveys, so in harmony with the friendship which has consistently moved the
                    Dominican Government in its relations with the United States.</p>
                <p>Accept [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Huntington Wilson.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
